      "description": "The outer modal operator K (Reinhardt's B) is missing from the formalized sentence. Reinhardt's Theorem 5 asserts the inconsistency of ∃e B∀x(Bp(x) ↔ U(e,x)) (proved via ∃e ∀x B(Bp(x) ↔ U(e,x))), and the author's claim likewise specifies ∃e B∀x(B¬U(x,x) ↔ U(e,x)). However, Def16 is ∀x₀ (K(¬U(x₀,x₀)) ↔ U(x₁,x₀)) and Target asserts derivability of neg (ex 1 Def16), i.e. ¬∃x₁ ∀x₀ (K(¬U(x₀,x₀)) ↔ U(x₁,x₀)), with no K outside ∀x₀ or the biconditional. Without that outer K, the sentence is consistent in Def14 (it holds at the root of a two-world reflexive-transitive constant-domain Kripke model with singleton domain {0} where U(0,0) is false at the root and true at the accessible world), making Target false for T = ∅."
    },
